      "message": "Is there a reason this code lives here in IpServer? Could we instead just add something like this to BpfCoordinator?\n\n    public void handleNeighborEvent(IpServer ipServer, NeighborEvent e)\n\nor:\n\n    public void handleNeighborEvent(MacAddress localMacAddr, NeighborEvent e)\n\n\nI think that would let you delete some of the code here and would in general be simpler. If it\u0027s easy and quick I would do that in this CL. If not, add a TODO.\n\n\nLong term, I think the IPv6 code should probably move to BpfCoordinator as well (but no need to do this now). The IPv6 part would probably look something like this:\n\n    public void handleIPv6UpstreamChanged(IpServer ipServer, int oldIfindex, int newIfindex) {\n\n    public void handleUpstreamRemoved(IpServer ipServer) {\n\nOnce that\u0027s done you could move the IPv6 forwarding rules to BpfCoordinator as well.",
